WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.119 --> 00:00:13.234
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:14.943 --> 00:00:18.885
I can't believe I cleared out
that whole hallway for nothing.

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:20.782
This is such a waste, too.

00:00:20.782 --> 00:00:24.933
I mean, the military is barely doing
its job, but they could outsource this.

00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:27.972
Make a public announcement that
every gun owner is welcome

00:00:27.972 --> 00:00:31.649
to come here and shoot aliens.
Kill as many as you want.

00:00:31.649 --> 00:00:34.951
Militias dream of something
like this happening.

00:00:34.951 --> 00:00:38.246
If we open this up, it would be
like a modern-day pilgrimage

00:00:38.246 --> 00:00:39.749
for a third of the country.

00:00:39.749 --> 00:00:42.534
Hey, maybe there's a drainage pipe here.

00:00:45.615 --> 00:00:50.400
[underwater mumbling]

00:00:51.995 --> 00:00:52.724
[inhale]

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.842
[underwater mumbling]

00:00:56.842 --> 00:00:58.450
Gaaah... dahh!

00:00:59.115 --> 00:00:59.901
Bleugh...

00:01:00.529 --> 00:01:02.872
Oh, I forgot about this thing.

00:01:02.872 --> 00:01:05.313
So, what's this valve do?
Drain the pond?

00:01:05.313 --> 00:01:09.567
Yeah, why not? I don't even
have to touch the egg sac...

00:01:10.138 --> 00:01:11.843
Okay, let's...

00:01:11.843 --> 00:01:13.122
[snarks chirping]
...shit.

00:01:13.122 --> 00:01:15.486
NO! RUH-YAH-YAH-YAH-YAH-YAH-YAH-YAH...!

00:01:15.486 --> 00:01:17.801
Friggin'... popcorn bugs!

00:01:18.537 --> 00:01:21.269
Well, that actually went
better than I thought,

00:01:21.269 --> 00:01:26.514
because, besides the fact that I don't have
a screaming insect thing biting my face,

00:01:26.514 --> 00:01:30.727
it look like that doesn't drain the pond
but opened up a hatchway instead.

00:01:30.727 --> 00:01:34.957
I guess it's sealed so that water
doesn't seep in when it rains

00:01:34.957 --> 00:01:40.295
and floods the underground manmade
pond here with no source of water,

00:01:40.295 --> 00:01:43.500
and this all makes sense
because we're in the desert.

00:01:44.638 --> 00:01:46.532
Okay, so...

00:01:46.532 --> 00:01:49.283
I feel like there's
something I should be doing.

00:01:49.283 --> 00:01:50.548
[laser chirps, turret whines]
Whoa-WHOA!

00:01:50.548 --> 00:01:54.323
[turret firing]

00:01:54.323 --> 00:01:57.262
Okay, it's more about what I
should NOT be doing!

00:01:57.262 --> 00:01:59.702
Not being shot hasn't changed!

00:01:59.702 --> 00:02:00.722
It was true yesterday,

00:02:00.722 --> 00:02:03.000
[turret firing]
it's still true today!

00:02:03.792 --> 00:02:04.875
[turret firing]

00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:09.207
In fact, that's a life lesson you can
take with you: Don't get shot. Ever.

00:02:09.207 --> 00:02:10.892
[turret firing]

00:02:10.892 --> 00:02:12.543
[turret whirring down]

00:02:12.543 --> 00:02:15.031
I am glad this thing shot
the aliens, though,

00:02:15.031 --> 00:02:18.509
and it's not specifically
programmed to only shoot me,

00:02:18.509 --> 00:02:21.434
because, frankly, that wouldn't
surprise me at this point.

00:02:23.182 --> 00:02:28.000
Okay, this runs west to east, but I don't
even know which way I've been going.

00:02:28.422 --> 00:02:29.701
I'll ask for directions.

00:02:32.191 --> 00:02:33.634
He doesn't know either.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.467
I'm gonna go another way.

00:02:37.031 --> 00:02:40.370
Okay... but these tunnels are
completely gated off.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:43.017
So, yeah, that was a simple decision.

00:02:43.017 --> 00:02:45.776
I wonder if I'm being herded
towards more danger.

00:02:45.776 --> 00:02:48.667
I mean, of course I am, but I
wonder if it's deliberate.

00:02:49.644 --> 00:02:50.100
Shit...

00:02:50.698 --> 00:02:52.003
[gagging]

00:02:52.697 --> 00:02:54.976
It was water all along.

00:02:57.781 --> 00:03:01.349
If I ever get out of here or
find a copy of the blueprints,

00:03:01.349 --> 00:03:06.395
I bet I'm going to discover I've took the
longest possible path through the facility.

00:03:06.395 --> 00:03:10.419
Some architect will look at the map
and say, "Oh, you took THAT tunnel.

00:03:10.419 --> 00:03:12.567
"Yeah, that added two miles to your route."

00:03:13.097 --> 00:03:14.853
[low rumbling]

00:03:14.853 --> 00:03:16.011
What was that?

00:03:16.011 --> 00:03:16.801
Hey, what...?

00:03:18.794 --> 00:03:21.534
Yep. Another shark. Of course.

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:23.167
Hello!

00:03:24.314 --> 00:03:26.524
Yeah, I'm dead certain there
were sharks here

00:03:26.524 --> 00:03:29.211
before this whole teleportation madness.

00:03:29.211 --> 00:03:32.300
I mean, I saw a shark cage;
what more proof do I need?

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:34.527
[ichthyosaur moans]

00:03:34.527 --> 00:03:36.523
Yeah! You stay back in the pool!

00:03:36.523 --> 00:03:38.993
Nobody's evolving legs on my watch!

00:03:38.993 --> 00:03:43.007
Hey, that part looks shallow; maybe
I don't HAVE to be a shark-hunter.

00:03:43.007 --> 00:03:45.133
That would definitely reduce my stress.

00:03:47.753 --> 00:03:50.767
Besides, what's the point if I
don't have a trophy to show people?

00:03:51.825 --> 00:03:52.684
Yaah...

00:03:54.027 --> 00:03:55.652
I can't get the carcass stuffed;

00:03:55.652 --> 00:03:58.567
people will have to take me at
my word I've killed sharks.

00:04:00.214 --> 00:04:01.601
I don't want to be that guy.

00:04:02.144 --> 00:04:05.346
Holy crap, it's a Charlie Chaplin cog.

00:04:05.346 --> 00:04:07.667
So, it's either this or the shark, huh?

00:04:08.465 --> 00:04:10.901
Oh, there's a gap. This is slow moving.

00:04:11.555 --> 00:04:13.000
[underwater mumbling]

00:04:16.223 --> 00:04:17.033
[inhale]

00:04:18.379 --> 00:04:21.467
[underwater mumbling]

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:23.634
WORMS!

00:04:24.134 --> 00:04:28.267
[underwater panicking]

00:04:31.084 --> 00:04:34.121
Bah! I am Captain Hydroelectric.

00:04:34.121 --> 00:04:36.176
At least I assume that's
what this place is for.

00:04:36.176 --> 00:04:37.914
[lock jiggles]
Why is this locked?

00:04:37.914 --> 00:04:41.167
This place is pretty remote; I
bet there's skeletons inside.

00:04:42.687 --> 00:04:45.267
Ah! I hope I can find some gold teeth.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.810
Oh, so there's NOTHING.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:52.159
Yeah, I guess that should've
been my first guess.

00:04:52.159 --> 00:04:56.848
Y'know, I have found explosives
just lying on shelves or in boxes,

00:04:56.848 --> 00:05:00.067
but a hidden padlocked door
contains absolutely nothing.

00:05:01.203 --> 00:05:03.591
I guess the idea is things are more secure

00:05:03.591 --> 00:05:07.566
if you do the exact opposite of
what you should do?

00:05:07.566 --> 00:05:08.334
Hm.

00:05:10.721 --> 00:05:12.169
What the hell is this?

00:05:12.169 --> 00:05:13.599
[chomping sound]
Hey!

00:05:13.599 --> 00:05:17.641
[underwater panicking]

00:05:17.641 --> 00:05:20.496
I'VE GOTTA GET OUT OF THE WATER!
WORMS EVERYWHERE!

00:05:20.496 --> 00:05:22.002
WORMS ARE GONNA GET ME!

00:05:22.002 --> 00:05:22.883
No, c'mon...

00:05:22.883 --> 00:05:23.690
[straining]
Okay... gaahhh...

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.419
[choking]

00:05:25.419 --> 00:05:26.776
...c'mon! ...daah! ...gaaaahhhh!

00:05:26.776 --> 00:05:28.294
[gasping]

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:29.834
JESUS CHRIST!

00:05:30.224 --> 00:05:33.124
Are these worms even real or
am I just going through withdrawal

00:05:33.124 --> 00:05:35.234
because I'm a bigger alcoholic
than I thought?

00:05:36.079 --> 00:05:39.266
I don't drink THAT much,
that's what pills are for.

00:05:39.266 --> 00:05:42.082
And, what the hell?
This gear isn't turning anything!

00:05:42.082 --> 00:05:45.700
It's not just out of sync, there's
literally nothing for it to turn!

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:49.680
It's not a water wheel... there's
no damned point to this thing at all!

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:55.027
Oh, wait, I see. It must be here to crush
the shark if it tries to swim up here.

00:05:55.027 --> 00:05:56.237
I get it now.

00:05:56.237 --> 00:05:58.601
Ah, okay. Paper beats rock.

00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:00.550
Hand-grenade beats unmanned sentry g--

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:01.200
Shit.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:08.767
Okay... that... was the rehearsal,
so now let's do the real thing. Yeah!

00:06:09.628 --> 00:06:13.858
Y'know, I'm getting pretty tired of these
explosives that don't actually do anything.

00:06:13.858 --> 00:06:15.324
Was there a mix-up at the factory

00:06:15.324 --> 00:06:18.856
and some kid with fireworks is getting
his hands blown off right now?

00:06:18.856 --> 00:06:20.734
All right, let's do this the hard way.

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:24.813
[turret whirrs down]

00:06:24.813 --> 00:06:27.729
Maybe the grenades are like the
bullets in Starship Troopers

00:06:27.729 --> 00:06:31.508
where they train with blanks but
every 10,000th round is real.

00:06:31.508 --> 00:06:33.167
So, it's like that, but in reverse.

00:06:34.136 --> 00:06:39.400
[ichthyosaur growls]
[underwater mumbling]

00:06:42.573 --> 00:06:46.167
[ichthyosaur growls]
[underwater mumbling]

00:06:46.685 --> 00:06:48.689
Yeah, that shark's pretty wound up.

00:06:48.689 --> 00:06:51.790
I'm getting out of the water before
it figures out how to jump the fence.

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:53.738
Getting shot makes me upset, too.

00:06:53.738 --> 00:06:56.647
Oh, maybe he's here to feed the shark.

00:06:56.647 --> 00:06:58.133
Well, I can't endorse that.

00:06:59.505 --> 00:07:01.934
GO BACK! THE SHARK'S NOT WORTH IT!

00:07:03.144 --> 00:07:03.669
[grenade clatters]

00:07:03.669 --> 00:07:04.471
Uh...

00:07:04.471 --> 00:07:05.630
[explosion]

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:06.467
Christ.

00:07:09.337 --> 00:07:12.499
NOW, YOUR DYING WISH MAYBE FOR
ME TO FEED YOU TO THE SHARK,

00:07:12.499 --> 00:07:15.400
BUT I'M NOT GOING TO DO IT!
YOU'RE BETTER OFF LEAVING!

00:07:16.562 --> 00:07:19.648
Y'see? Man, I'm not even
sure this guy was military.

00:07:19.648 --> 00:07:22.699
Maybe he's just a PETA-extremist
that snuck in here.

00:07:22.699 --> 00:07:25.969
Oh. Rockets. Oh, wow.

00:07:25.969 --> 00:07:28.605
Yeah, I'll try and strap some
more of these to me.

00:07:28.605 --> 00:07:31.036
Ahh, I don't think I can hold any more.

00:07:31.036 --> 00:07:34.467
I'll just need to find an excuse
to use a rocket launcher.

00:07:35.382 --> 00:07:37.400
I could think of a lot of excuses.

00:07:38.078 --> 00:07:39.767
Okay, looks clear enough.

00:07:41.365 --> 00:07:43.267
[plane whines, distant explosions]
God, they're still bombing?

00:07:45.018 --> 00:07:47.218
Well, these guys don't seem
concerned about that,

00:07:47.218 --> 00:07:49.354
so that means I'm either
clear of the bombing

00:07:49.354 --> 00:07:51.467
[plane whines, distant explosions]
or else, they're incredibly stupid.

00:07:52.115 --> 00:07:53.000
Hmm.

00:07:55.747 --> 00:07:56.534
Daahhh!

00:07:59.060 --> 00:07:59.834
GAAAAH!

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:03.200
[plane whines, closer explosions]
Oh, shit! That's a tank!

00:08:05.042 --> 00:08:07.096
I wonder if anyone's operating it?

00:08:07.096 --> 00:08:08.734
Well, why take a chance?

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:11.944
Guess not.

00:08:11.944 --> 00:08:12.847
[explosion]

00:08:12.847 --> 00:08:14.556
[ears ringing]
RAAAGH!

00:08:14.556 --> 00:08:17.300
[ears ringing]
C'MON, MAN! YOU TRYIN' TO HURT MY EARS?!

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:22.026
[plane whines, explosions]
OH, YEAH!

00:08:22.026 --> 00:08:24.300
But, I'm still not convinced.

00:08:26.507 --> 00:08:28.784
Okay, now I'm more convinced.

00:08:28.784 --> 00:08:31.741
Now, a lesser man might
keep moving blindly,

00:08:31.741 --> 00:08:35.406
but I am a man of vision and
I have seen more rockets.

00:08:35.406 --> 00:08:39.139
I mean, literally; I have some vacancies
now and I haven't forgotten about those.

00:08:39.139 --> 00:08:40.442
[cockroach crunches]
Yuck.

00:08:40.442 --> 00:08:42.803
Now I can keep moving blindly.

00:08:42.803 --> 00:08:46.164
Speaking of blind, why did the soldiers
both have their backs toward me

00:08:46.164 --> 00:08:50.533
when I came out of the hole even
though the tank was facing my direction?

00:08:50.533 --> 00:08:54.103
I mean, it clearly looks like they're
trying to guard this end of the road;

00:08:54.103 --> 00:08:56.118
the tank wouldn't be there otherwise.

00:08:56.118 --> 00:08:59.443
Maybe it's some interpretive
form of guard duty hopscotch.

00:08:59.443 --> 00:09:02.734
This job probably gets pretty boring
without me to come spice things up.

00:09:03.429 --> 00:09:05.400
[turret whines]
WHOO-BA-DEE-BOOP-BOP-BOW!

00:09:06.648 --> 00:09:11.067
Well, it works both ways; they find plenty
of ways to keep my day interesting as well.

00:09:11.655 --> 00:09:12.934
All right, let's do this.

00:09:13.402 --> 00:09:15.224
[gibbering]

00:09:15.224 --> 00:09:18.133
I hate playing peek-a-boo with
this thing; there's no emotion.

00:09:19.048 --> 00:09:20.167
Totally cold.

00:09:20.825 --> 00:09:22.153
This AI is shit.

00:09:22.153 --> 00:09:24.334
This is why robots are never
going to rule the world.

00:09:25.031 --> 00:09:27.913
Robots are only good at
highly-specific tasks.

00:09:27.913 --> 00:09:31.958
We only wish they would take over
the world. Then we wouldn't have to.

00:09:31.958 --> 00:09:35.019
But then, we're the ones that would have
to program them, so what the hell?

00:09:35.019 --> 00:09:37.093
[muzak]

00:09:37.093 --> 00:09:38.142
[muzak]
Is this a trap?

00:09:38.142 --> 00:09:39.410
[muzak]

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:40.488
[muzak]
Yeah, probably.

00:09:40.488 --> 00:09:44.170
[muzak]

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.330
[muzak]
This music really doesn't

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:46.701
[muzak]
match my mood right now.

00:09:46.701 --> 00:09:50.676
[muzak]

00:09:50.676 --> 00:09:53.048
[muzak]
Battery life on robots suck, too.

00:09:53.048 --> 00:09:58.367
[muzak]

